<p>A profile is seen as a 40-pixel circle, so it is one thing and one mark. Three to pick from, all drawn: the illustration on cream, with its own golden circle (the one the channel art uses, so the two agree); the brand’s square, the S and the dot, which is the avatar that matches the favicon; or a photograph inside a hairline ring. On all three the recording-light dot sits top right, in the accent — the same dot the logo carries.</p>
